# SSH Public Key Directory

To use SSH key-based authentication (recommended), add your public SSH key here.

This allows passwordless SSH login to the Raspberry Pi after boot.

## Steps

```bash
# 1. On the client machine (laptop/desktop), generate an SSH key if you don't have one
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "your_email@example.com"

# 2. Display the public key
cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub

# 3. Paste the public key into this file
vi external/board/raspberrypi/rootfs-overlay/root/.ssh/authorized_keys

# 4. Rebuild the system image and deploy
make buildroot
sudo make deploy